  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1021 PM MDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nScattered to numerous thunderstorms expected tomorrow with almost \nall locations having a good chance to see a storm. Biggest threat \nwill be severe wind gusts from outflows (58+ mph). Some potential \nfor isolated severe hail (1\"+). Flash flooding threat looks greatest \nover the Sacramento Mtns and Otero Mesa, and a lower threat (but \nstill possible) elsewhere across the CWA. Activity looks to persist \ninto the early overnight hours before moving into Mexico overnight. \nUpper high pressure continues to meander over the desert southwest \nthrough around mid-week next week allowing for a rebound in \ntemperatures back to the triple digits for a good portion of the \ndesert lowlands starting Monday. Daily thunderstorm chances exist \nwith a focus over the area mountains and western locations.",
